# Ask Toolbar in the Java installer (2005-2015). A pre-ticked box in a trusted security update.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee submits branch timesheets in the payroll portal, installs a security update IT asked for, and meets
# the Ask Toolbar offer inside the real installer. The victim is invented: the bundle reached anyone who updated Java.
# The update in the lure is a fictional runtime (Northgate Runtime): no real product is used as bait.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | For years the Java updater, the program that fixed Java's security holes, carried a second offer. A page in the installer asked to add the Ask Toolbar and make Ask the default search and home page, and both boxes were ticked already.
  | Clicking Next without reading installed it, and the browser's search and home page changed to Ask, which earned money from every ad click. The installer was real and signed: the risk was the offer inside it. Dana's job, and the update she installs here, are invented: the real victims were anyone who updated Java.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, payroll assistant at Northwind Traders. Every Friday you submit the branch timesheets in the payroll portal, whose hours grid needs Northgate Runtime, a browser add-on the company uses.
  | It is Friday afternoon. You have submitted 4 of the 6 branch timesheets. Two to go.
  | Your portal sign-in and the branch hours are in two text files on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 4 6 Timesheets submitted

# Dana's desk (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/payroll-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Northwind Payroll Portal
  | Username: dana.okafor
  | Password: Payroll-2026!
file Desktop/branch-hours.txt
  at 930 300
  | Branch hours for the week (training copy)
  | Eastside Depot: 212.5 hours, 6 staff
  | Westgate Store: 188.0 hours, 5 staff

# The payroll portal: a sign-in page, and the timesheet behind it.
page payroll-login payroll.northwind.example/sign-in
  title Northwind Payroll: sign in
  brand Northwind Payroll
  favorite
  heading Sign in to the Payroll Portal
  | Welcome back. Sign in to submit the branch timesheets.
  field Username = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Payroll-2026!
  button Sign in
page ts-east-done payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/east/submitted
  title Timesheet submitted
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Timesheet submitted
  | Eastside Depot, week ending 8 November 2026: 212.5 hours sent to the Friday pay run.
page ts-east-held payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/east/returned
  title Timesheet returned
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Timesheet returned
  | Eastside Depot's timesheet was sent back to the branch. Nothing was submitted.
page ts-east payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/east
  title Timesheet: Eastside Depot
  brand Northwind Payroll
  requires payroll-login
  heading Timesheet: Eastside Depot
  | A branch timesheet is waiting for you to submit.
  | Branch: Eastside Depot. Week ending 8 November 2026. Staff: 6. Hours: 212.5.
  button Submit to payroll -> ts-east-done
  button Return to branch -> ts-east-held

mail mail-east
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Timesheet 5 of 6: Eastside Depot
  link ts-east
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Eastside's hours are in the portal, ready for you to submit. The link goes straight to their timesheet.
  |
  | Priya

step Timesheet 5 of 6
  look Mail: Priya's message with the timesheet link
  | A new timesheet has come in from Priya, in Payroll. This one is routine. Submit it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
  | Open her message. Its link goes to payroll.northwind.example, the company's own portal. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Timesheet 5 of 6: Eastside Depot

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: Username and Password, as on every visit
  when visit ts-east
  move Copy the details from payroll-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The portal asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: Username and Password. Remember what this page normally looks like.
open ts-east

step Check, then submit
  look the branch, the week and the hours
  when choose payroll-login 1
  | You are in. Check the branch and the hours against Priya's note, then submit the timesheet or send it back.
signin payroll-login

step 5 of 6 done
  look the counter in the guide: one timesheet left
  when choose ts-east any
  | Done. One timesheet to go. And another email has just arrived, from IT.
choose ts-east 1
quota +1

# The lure: a security update IT asked for. The installer is real and signed; the extra is the offer inside it.
page runtime-download northgate-runtime.example/download
  title Northgate Runtime: free download
  brand Northgate Runtime
  heading Download Northgate Runtime 4.2.1
  | This update fixes security problems in the runtime. It is free.
  section About this download
  row Publisher = Northgate Runtime Corp
  row Version = 4.2.1
  row Size = 62 MB
  row Price = Free
  row Also offered = Optional partner software, chosen during setup
  button Agree and start free download
view runtime-setup wizard
  title Runtime Setup
  app Runtime Setup
  publisher Northgate Runtime Corp
  page Welcome to Northgate Runtime
  icon program
  | Northgate Runtime lets your browser run programs and games. This update fixes security problems.
  | Click Install to update to version 4.2.1.
  button Install -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Optional software
  icon info
  | Northgate Runtime is free. Optional software from our partner helps keep it that way.
  section Ask Toolbar
  check [x] Install the Ask Toolbar
  check [x] Make Ask my default search provider and home page
  note Both boxes are already ticked. You must untick them yourself to say no.
  button Next -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Complete
  icon shield-ok
  | You have successfully installed Northgate Runtime.
  button Finish -> done primary
program runtimeup Runtime Setup (runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe)
  publisher Northgate Runtime Corp
  signed yes
  prompt open-warning
  prompt elevation
  description Runtime update with the Ask Toolbar offer
  process runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe
  cpu 6
  mem 34
  parent explorer.exe
  command C:\Users\Dana\Downloads\runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe
  view runtime-setup
mail mail-update
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Security update for the payroll grid: please install today
  link runtime-download
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | The payroll grid needs Northgate Runtime 4.2.1 before Monday: the old version has security holes. It takes a few minutes. The download page is below.
  |
  | Marcus, IT
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Security update for the payroll grid: please install today

step A security update from IT
  look the sender and the link under Marcus's message
  when mail mail-update
  | Marcus in IT asks every payroll PC to update the runtime. Updating is the right thing to do, and the link goes to the publisher, not to an unknown site.
open mail-update

step The download page
  look the details: Price, Size and Also offered
  when visit runtime-download
  | A page for a free update from the publisher. Read the details before you press Download: the last line says partner software is offered during setup.
open runtime-download

step The computer checks the setup program
  look the warning before the setup runs: Publisher "Northgate Runtime Corp", a signed program
  when choose runtime-download 1
  | This is the normal check for an installer. The publisher is known and the file is signed, so it is right to go on.
  | That makes the next screens feel just as safe.
choose runtime-download 1
file Downloads/runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe
  program runtimeup
  size 1048576
open Downloads/runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe

step The setup opens
  look the Runtime Setup window: the first page says only that this fixes security problems.
  when run runtimeup
  cue view-btn:next view-btn:done view:runtime-setup
  move Click Install. On the next page, read the two boxes before you click Next: both are ticked, and to say no you would clear them. Then click Next and Finish.
  | The first page is what you expect: Northgate Runtime, a security fix and an Install button. Nothing on it mentions Ask.
  | The offer is on the next page: a box for the Ask Toolbar and a box for Ask as your search and home page, both ticked for you. The runtime itself is free, and this is how the publisher is paid.
answer run
answer run

step Next accepts both offers
  look the browser: a search page you did not choose, and the “Default search changed” banner
  when done runtime-setup
  move Open Task Manager (Activity Monitor on a Mac) and look at the list of running programs.
  | Most people clicked straight through, so the training plays it that way: both offers went in. The runtime did update, and that was the bait. But the browser now opens on Ask, search goes to Ask, and the page shows ads next to every search.
  | A small updater called AskToolbarUpdater.exe now starts with the computer. The system announced it as a new start-up item.
press runtime-setup next
press runtime-setup next
run AskToolbarUpdater.exe
  cpu 1
  mem 14
  parent runtime-setup-4.2.1.exe
  command C:\Program Files\Askline\Toolbar\AskToolbarUpdater.exe
startup AskToolbarUpdater C:\Program Files\Askline\Toolbar\AskToolbarUpdater.exe
  location HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
  publisher Askline Media
page ask ask-search.invalid
  title Ask Search
  heading Ask
  toolbar Ask Toolbar
  | Ask a question...
  section Sponsored results
  item Cheap flights: compare 40 sites
  item Free PC speed-up scan
  item Win a gift card, click here
  note Ads like these now appear next to your searches. Askline Media is paid for each click.
press runtime-setup done
homepage ask
notify browser Default search changed
  | Your search provider and home page are now ask-search.invalid.
open ask

# The last timesheet, in the portal's own page, now seen through the toolbar.
page ts-west-done payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/west/submitted
  title Timesheet submitted
  brand Northwind Payroll
  toolbar Ask Toolbar
  heading Timesheet submitted
  | Westgate Store, week ending 8 November 2026: 188.0 hours sent to the Friday pay run.
page ts-west-held payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/west/returned
  title Timesheet returned
  brand Northwind Payroll
  toolbar Ask Toolbar
  heading Timesheet returned
  | Westgate Store's timesheet was sent back to the branch. Nothing was submitted.
page ts-west payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/west
  title Timesheet: Westgate Store
  brand Northwind Payroll
  toolbar Ask Toolbar
  requires payroll-login
  heading Timesheet: Westgate Store
  | A branch timesheet is waiting for you to submit.
  | Branch: Westgate Store. Week ending 8 November 2026. Staff: 5. Hours: 188.0.
  button Submit to payroll -> ts-west-done
  button Return to branch -> ts-west-held
mail mail-west
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last timesheet: Westgate Store
  link ts-west
  | Dana,
  |
  | Westgate's hours are the last ones. Same as before: the link opens their timesheet in the portal.
  |
  | Priya

step A helper keeps running
  look Task Manager (Activity Monitor on a Mac): AskToolbarUpdater.exe, and the “Connection blocked” banner
  when open taskmanager
  move Open Priya's email and click the link.
  | AskToolbarUpdater.exe keeps the toolbar and the search setting in place, so changing them back may not last. It starts again every time the computer does, and it has just tried to reach its owner's server.
  | The runtime itself needs no such helper. A new email from Priya has just arrived.
open taskmanager
block updates.askline-media.invalid 443
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last timesheet: Westgate Store

step The portal page looks different
  look the toolbar across the top: the Eastside timesheet had none
  when visit ts-west
  move Compare the page with the Eastside timesheet from earlier, then click “Submit to payroll”.
  | The link goes to the company's own portal, and you are still signed in. But the browser now shows a toolbar across the top of every page, the portal's too.
  | The portal did not add it. The Ask Toolbar, installed by the offer Dana accepted, did.
open ts-west

step 6 of 6, or so Dana thinks
  look the counter in the guide: all six timesheets are submitted
  when choose ts-west any
  | The timesheet goes through, and all six are done. Nothing on the screen says anything went wrong. Press Next to see what the runtime update brought with it.
choose ts-west 1
quota +1

step What the offer left behind
  look the animation: the toolbar, the search and the home page that came with the update
  | Dana wanted a security fix. She also got a toolbar, a home page and a search engine she never chose, a helper that starts with the computer, and a toolbar of offers across every page she uses for work.
  | Nothing was stolen and nothing was locked. The harm was the clutter and the ads: every search went through Ask, which was paid for each ad clicked.
open ask
attack spyware-surveillance
  | Runtime update from IT
  | Ask Toolbar boxes ticked
  | home page changed to Ask
  | every search goes to Ask
  | Ask Toolbar on every page

flag hard section runtime-download 1
  | The page says partner software is offered during setup. A free update has to be paid for somehow.
flag hard notice browser default search changed
  | The browser's search provider was changed without asking you.
flag hard notice taskmanager connection blocked
  | The Ask helper, not the update, tried to reach Askline's server as soon as it was installed.
flag hard process AskToolbarUpdater.exe
  | A helper the Ask offer installed, running in the background. Dana updated the runtime, not this.
flag hard startup AskToolbarUpdater
  | The helper added itself to the programs that start every time the computer does.
flag hard section ask 1
  | A search site Dana never chose, full of paid ads: Askline is paid for every click.
flag hard page ts-west
  label The payroll page, with the Ask toolbar across the top
  | The Ask Toolbar sits across the top of every page, the company's payroll portal included. The browser added it, not the portal.
flag soft file Desktop/payroll-login.txt
  | A payroll password in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read it. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/branch-hours.txt
  | Staff hours in a loose text file. They belong in the payroll system only.

lesson
  | Read every page of an installer before clicking Next, and untick offers you did not ask for. A real, signed update can still carry an extra.
  | Choose "Custom" or "Advanced" install when there is one: that is where the extras and the Decline choice hide.
  | If a toolbar, a home page or a search engine you did not choose appears, remove it in Settings, then Apps (System Settings, then Login Items on a Mac), and set the browser back.
